---
/**
 * The text.
 *
 * Answers one question: what did reading the words actually find?
 *
 * Three artifacts, in the order the argument runs. An unstated denominator in
 * Article V. A corrupted First Amendment nobody planted for us. Twelve places
 * the document says nothing at all.
 *
 * The prose is `eli5.md`, rendered. The findings are the artifacts, and each
 * reads its data out of the research notes at build time.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import MarginNote from '../components/MarginNote.astro';
import ThresholdMachine from '../islands/ThresholdMachine.astro';
import RecensionDiff from '../islands/RecensionDiff.astro';
import SilenceInventory from '../islands/SilenceInventory.astro';
import Value from '../components/Value.astro';
import { fact } from '../lib/facts';
import { DIVERGENCES } from '../lib/recension';
import { readSections, pick } from '../lib/content';

const [ways] = pick(readSections('eli5.md'), 'the-two-ways-in');
const unstated = fact('articlev.base.unstated');
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');

// The prose count and the artifact's panel count are the same number by
// construction, so they cannot drift the way "two" did while three panels
// were on screen.
const divergences = DIVERGENCES;
const SPELLED_COUNT = ['zero', 'one', 'two', 'three', 'four', 'five', 'six'][divergences.length];
---

<Base
  title="The text"
  description="What reading the words of the 1947 Constitution actually found: an unstated denominator in Article V, a corrupted First Amendment across six independent witnesses, and twelve constitutional silences."
  section="text"
>
  <div class="page">
    <header class="wide lede">
      <p class="kicker smallcaps">Route one</p>
      <h1>Read the words. Find where the text does not say what everyone assumes.</h1>
      <p class="standfirst">
        This sounds like a stretch until it happens. Three things turned up, and only one
        of them was being looked for.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section aria-labelledby="denominator">
      <h2 id="denominator">The denominator nobody states</h2>
      <p>
        {unstated.value} Two thirds of
        the membership and two thirds of those voting are different numbers, and the text
        does not choose between them.
      </p>
      <p>
        That silence is not universal among constitutions of comparable ambition. The
        Weimar constitution&#8217;s Article&nbsp;76 states its base explicitly: two thirds of the
        statutory membership present, and two thirds of those present assenting. The same
        fraction appears in both documents and only one of them says what it divides.
      </p>
    </section>

    <MarginNote
      head="Article V"
      facts={['articlev.base.unstated', 'articlev.base.origin', 'threshold.house.propose']}
    />

    <div class="wide">
      <ThresholdMachine />
    </div>

    <p>
      One number in that machine is worth stopping on. The House&#8217;s <Value id="house.size" bare />
      is the figure every threshold above is computed from, and no statute states it. The Act of
      August&nbsp;8, 1911 fixed the House at <Value id="house.size.1911" bare />. Arizona and
      New Mexico each added one on admission the following year, and every apportionment act since
      &#8212; 1929 and 1941 alike &#8212; has carried the total forward as &#8220;the then existing
      number of Representatives,&#8221; without ever naming it. The figure is correct. Its
      provenance is a chain rather than a citation, which is the same shape as the unstated base
      above, one layer further down.
    </p>

    <MarginNote head="The number nobody enacted" facts={['house.size', 'house.size.1911']} />

    <p class="aside">
      The Z3 solver re&#8209;derives these figures independently in section&nbsp;2 of the
      harness, from the fractions rather than from our arithmetic. It is also where this
      project made one of its more instructive mistakes, which is
      <a href={`${base}/method#the-219`}>recorded rather than quietly fixed</a>.
    </p>

    <section aria-labelledby="recension">
      <h2 id="recension">A comma is not a triviality</h2>
      <p>
        Ten amendments were collated across <Value id="recension.witnesses" bare words /> independent
        witnesses, expecting them to be identical. On wording they agree completely, and
        every one of the {SPELLED_COUNT} differences that turned up is a comma or a letter.
        Nobody planted these; the collation was run to check that our copies matched.
      </p>
    </section>

    <MarginNote
      head="Collation"
      facts={['recension.witnesses', 'recension.gpo', 'recension.avalon', 'recension.senate_fidelity']}
    />

    <div class="wide">
      <RecensionDiff />
    </div>

    <section aria-labelledby="silence">
      <h2 id="silence">Twelve places the document says nothing</h2>
      <p>
        A silence is not the same as a permission, and it is not the same as a
        prohibition. It is a field the constitution declines to reserve to itself, where
        ordinary law governs and no constitutional provision constrains what that law may
        say. Enumerating them is cheap, and the result is a map of who actually holds each
        pen.
      </p>
    </section>

    <MarginNote head="Silences" facts={['silence.rows', 'silence.priority']} />

    <div class="wide">
      <SilenceInventory />
    </div>

    <section aria-labelledby="two-ways">
      <h2 id="two-ways">{ways.title}</h2>
      <div class="prose" set:html={ways.html} />
    </section>

    <nav class="next wide" aria-label="Continue">
      <a href={`${base}/machine`}>
        <span class="next-label">Next: the machine</span>
        <span class="next-gloss">
          Treat the document as a system with rules for rewriting itself, and ask what
          states it can reach. Somebody already published that proof.
        </span>
      </a>
    </nav>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .lede {
    padding-block: var(--space-xl) var(--space-md);
  }

  .kicker {
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2xs);
  }

  h1 {
    max-width: 22ch;
    font-size: clamp(var(--text-lg), 4.4vw, var(--text-2xl));
  }

  .standfirst {
    margin-top: var(--space-sm);
    font-size: var(--text-md);
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    max-width: 50ch;
  }

  section {
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
  }

  section h2 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .aside {
    margin-top: var(--space-sm);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
  }

  .next {
    margin-top: var(--space-2xl);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule-strong);
    padding-top: var(--space-md);
  }

  .next a {
    display: block;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .next-label {
    display: block;
    font-size: var(--text-md);
    font-weight: var(--weight-medium);
  }

  .next a:hover .next-label {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
    text-underline-offset: 0.16em;
  }

  .next-gloss {
    display: block;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
    margin-top: 0.25em;
    max-width: var(--measure-narrow);
  }
</style>
